"""Finish thirty earlier coordinate sets with individual, explicitly noncanonical scenarios."""
from copy import deepcopy
from best_guess_helpers import current_data, change, write_revision, DATE
from research_helpers import assessment
D=current_data();changes=[]
rows=[
('culture-main',{'nonworking':(.6,[.2,.9],'Biological humanlike citizen scenario: many can avoid ongoing useful work, but voluntary science, care, art and service still count. No canon census is claimed.')},
'''Citizens and independent Minds share political decisions, while Minds operate much of the practical infrastructure. The existing positive control point recognizes voting and shared social agency, with a broad alternative toward AI power; it does not mean humans own obedient Minds. The best-guess nonworking fraction is substantial because necessities require no job, but useful voluntary research, care, art and service still count as work. The wide interval allows a much more active citizenry than a simple leisure label suggests. This is an editorial scenario for biological humanlike residents, not a census or a count of all machine citizens.'''),
('machine-stops-before-collapse',{'nonworking':(.55,[.2,.85],'All-age underground-resident scenario allows extensive automatic provision but counts attendants, lecturers, committees and useful communication as work.')},
'''Human committees and attendants remain part of the order, so technical dependence alone does not prove a conscious AI sovereign. The best-guess nonworking fraction is moderately high because provision requires little ordinary production labor, with a broad allowance for useful lectures, care, maintenance and administration. Intellectual activity can still be work when it contributes to others. The fraction is not inferred from time spent physically motionless in a room. These estimates describe living residents before collapse; later deaths and broken machinery cannot supply a population of perfectly leisured people. Coercive exclusion remains a limit on the material floor.'''),
('manna-australia',{'nonworking':(.55,[.2,.85],'Project-member all-age scenario under robotic provision; useful elective projects, care and collective administration remain work despite no wage requirement.')},
'''Member participation gives the project a strong shared-control interpretation, while access remains bounded to membership and available resources. The best-guess nonworking fraction is substantial but leaves considerable room for useful self-directed projects, care, research and administration. Resource credits are not a labor census, and choosing an activity freely does not make its output useless. The broad interval is an editorial scenario across members and dependents. It does not give identical protection to nonmembers elsewhere, equate every pleasurable activity with productive employment, or pretend that robots have eliminated every scarce resource. The project’s material entitlement and actual participation remain separate judgments.'''),
('evitable-conflict-earth',{'nonworking':(.3,[.1,.6],'All-age human scenario retains plant workers, administration, care and other useful labor under machine coordination; layoffs are not a full population count.')},
'''The zero-variant label records that plant workers, layoffs and actual labor needs persist under machine coordination. Economic management is not automatically release from employment. The best-guess nonworking fraction is therefore modest, allowing dependents and displaced people while retaining useful factory, care and administrative work. It is not derived from the number of governing Machines or one local disturbance. The source-based control point remains near autonomous machine authority, whereas the favorable guarantee estimate describes a protective orientation rather than an explicit unconditional benefit. These are provisional reference-led judgments, with no new full-story reading or canonical census claimed.'''),
('noon-earth',{'nonworking':(.4,[.1,.75],'Human all-age scenario with strong vocational participation: machines remove routine subsistence work but science, education, care, exploration and creative contribution persist.')},
'''Human councils and professional communities coordinate the shared system, so domestic automation is not a separate machine ruling class. The best-guess nonworking fraction stays moderate because useful vocations remain culturally important: science, exploration, education, care and creative contribution count even without wages. Free necessities alone cannot tell us how many residents choose such roles. The broad interval is an all-age human scenario, not a statistic extracted from a robot count or one protagonist’s career. The strong material floor is kept distinct from the frequency of useful activity, and technocratic influence remains a qualification to the shared-control point.'''),
('orwell-oceania',{'nonworking':(.15,[.02,.4],'All-age scenario under compulsory labor and scarcity; useful Party administration, production, care and informal survival are work, with dependents allowed.')},
'''This zero variant concerns a regime that can divert technical capacity toward domination and permanent scarcity while retaining extensive human work. The low best-guess nonworking fraction reflects that pressure, with children and other nonparticipants included. Production, care, administration and useful informal survival still count; ideological employment is not automatically harmless leisure. The interval is deliberately broad because the novel gives no all-population participation census. Neither misery nor the destruction of output makes every person a nonworker. Concentrated human command and weak material protection remain the supported structural judgments, while the numeric fraction is an openly editorial scenario.'''),
('midas-compulsory-consumption',{'nonworking':(.1,[0,.4],'Imposed consumption is treated here as an assigned social duty, consistent with the record’s metric. Useful professional and care roles persist; quota sizes do not produce a census.')},
'''The low nonworking best guess uses this record’s explicit convention that compulsory consumption is a socially assigned duty, rather than simply calling every consumer idle. Professional, care and administrative roles also continue. A wide interval allows people outside sustained duties and uncertainty about whether particular consumption tasks should count as useful work. The number is not the inverse of the factory workforce or the amount each caste must consume. Human quota authorities retain concentrated control despite enormous automatic output. This describes the compulsory phase only, keeping Morey Fry’s later change as a separate material model with a different relationship to obligation.'''),
('fallout-prewar-appalachia',{'nonworking':(.45,[.15,.8],'Regional all-age scenario permits substantial robot displacement while retaining remaining industrial, care, maintenance and informal work; company automation targets are not a census.')},
'''Corporate owners direct the mining machinery, placing control near concentrated human command. The best-guess nonworking fraction is substantial because displacement is real, but it retains repair, care, remaining industrial activity and informal survival as useful work. A company’s staffing target cannot be converted directly into the share of all Appalachian people working. The broad interval includes uncertainty about dependents and the ability to find other work. Weak guarantees mean losing a wage can mean hardship even while productive output continues. The record stops before nuclear destruction, and neither later corpses nor empty automated sites become a population enjoying leisure.'''),
('fallout-institute',{'nonworking':(.2,[.05,.55],'Born-human enclave scenario: many adults retain useful scientific, medical and managerial roles; children and other nonparticipants form the central minority. Synth labor remains disclosed separately.')},
'''Born-human scientists and managers retain concentrated authority over the enclave and its synth workforce. The low best-guess nonworking fraction reflects that many privileged adults still do useful research, medicine or administration even when service labor supplies their surroundings. Dependents and other nonparticipants remain included. The percentage is not computed by treating every working synth as an idle human, and the supporting synthetic persons’ oppression stays explicit. This is a narrow beneficiary population rather than a claim that the Commonwealth has become post-work. Neither scientific status nor comfortable provision alone establishes the actual frequency of chosen work, hence the broad editorial interval.'''),
('her-before-departure',{'guarantees':(.3,[-.4,.85],'No general entitlement is depicted; the central guess is a comfortable but purchase-dependent service economy, with a broad range for unseen benefits.'),'nonworking':(.3,[.1,.65],'Human urban all-age scenario retains professions, care and informal activity while digital assistance substitutes some tasks; protagonist employment is not a census.')},
'''The guarantee best guess places ordinary life somewhat toward purchase-dependent insecurity, with a wide interval because a consumer story does not explain public benefits. Human institutions and buyers still have influence, while independent AI agency complicates control. The modest nonworking estimate retains professions, care and informal contribution despite digital task substitution. It is not derived from one employed protagonist or commuters. This remains an interpretive zero variant before the AIs leave, rather than a fully demonstrated post-work economy. Their later departure is a different technical situation, and no guaranteed outcome for displaced workers or universal ownership of AI services is invented.'''),
('idiran-empire-before-defeat',{'guarantees':(.65,[0,1],'Hierarchical religious empire and subordinate populations suggest weak universal protection, but civilian entitlements are not specified.'),'nonworking':(.2,[.02,.6],'Biological-person all-age scenario retains military, administrative, productive and care work under rejected machine autonomy; no civilian census inferred from war scenes.')},
'''The weak guarantee best guess reflects hierarchical domination rather than an asserted imperial welfare law. Biological rulers retain control, using capable technology while rejecting independent machine sovereignty. The low nonworking scenario counts real military, administrative, productive and care roles, while allowing dependents and some elite leisure. It is not a civilian census derived from battle scenes. Idirans and subject populations are explicitly a biological-person proxy, so their activity is not silently presented as a human statistic. The zero variant concerns technical restraint and preserved organic authority, not a claim that every job could instantly be replaced or that employment protection motivated the religious policy.'''),
('algebraist-dwellers',{'nonworking':(.5,[.15,.85],'Biological Dweller all-age scenario permits broad freedom from subsistence work while counting elective knowledge, civic and care activity. Adult goods rights do not determine juvenile participation.')},
'''Shared civic agency and common goods support the positive control estimate, qualified by uncertain productive machinery and different life stages. The best-guess nonworking fraction is intermediate because status-seeking, knowledge gathering, civic duties and care can remain useful work even without a necessity wage. Adult access to Common goods does not supply a juvenile activity count or make every pursuit a job. Dwellers are a declared nonhuman biological proxy, and the wide interval reflects that unfamiliar denominator. The score separates material security from prestige and from the frequency of chosen activity, rather than treating expensive distinctions or a long life as proof of universal leisure.'''),
('algebraist-mercatoria',{'guarantees':(.8,[.25,1],'An imperial hierarchy suppressing machine intelligence plausibly provides weak universal protection, with unknown differences between ranks and worlds.'),'nonworking':(.25,[.05,.65],'All-age biological-population scenario retains administrative, productive, military and care work; no machine-war count is used as a civilian labor rate.')},
'''The guarantee best guess is weak because an imperial order with unequal ranks does not imply a common material floor, though exact local rights remain unknown. Concentrated biological institutions retain authority while suppressing machine intelligence. A modest nonworking estimate allows dependents and some elite leisure but keeps useful production, administration, care and military activity in the count. It is not derived from the number of capable AIs being persecuted or from a war passage. This zero variant is a technical-restraint comparison across a broad biological proxy population, with wide intervals rather than a claim that every subject world shares an identical employment or benefit policy.'''),
('caves-of-steel-earth-cities',{'nonworking':(.3,[.1,.65],'All-age City-resident scenario includes displaced and dependent people while retaining human service, care, administration and informal work; declassification is not identical to no useful activity.')},
'''Human classifications and institutional control keep production close to the concentrated end, despite extensive robot substitution. The modest nonworking best guess includes dependents and displaced people but still counts service, care, administration and useful informal work. A declassified family may lose status without every member doing no useful activity. The interval is therefore much wider than any simple substitution figure. The near-middle guarantee point recognizes real minimal food and accommodation while preserving the loss of comfort and choice. This record does not import Spacer abundance or treat every City resident as an autonomous owner of the machines that displace human jobs.'''),
('solaria-naked-sun',{'nonworking':(.45,[.1,.85],'Resident-human all-age scenario under massive robot support; professional specialties, estate oversight and care can still be useful work, so robot-to-human ratios are not a leisure census.')},
'''Resident estates disperse substantial local command over robots, though that privilege excludes outsiders and does not abolish hierarchy. The intermediate nonworking best guess leaves considerable room for useful human specialties, estate oversight, care and chosen projects despite enormous robot support. It is not calculated from the ratio of robots to people. A resident who freely practices a profession still works under this metric. The wide interval reflects uncertainty about ages and how universal ongoing specialties are. This point covers Baley’s visited Solaria, not later transformed descendants, and it does not grant robot servants the same rights as their supported human owners.'''),
('aurora-robots-of-dawn',{'nonworking':(.35,[.1,.8],'Auroran resident-human scenario permits strong technical assistance while retaining professional, creative, scientific and care roles; free robot access does not state how many work.')},
'''Public fallback access to a robot strengthens provision without establishing equal productive power in every respect. The best-guess nonworking fraction is moderate because professional, scientific, creative and care roles can remain important in a comfortable society. A freely chosen vocation still counts as useful work, and public robot access is not a census of participation. The broad interval permits both a largely active citizenry and much wider leisure than the protagonists show. Human institutions and personal owners retain agency, so automatic service does not become a sovereign AI government. The resident scope also does not give every outside human the same right to settle or obtain support.'''),
('midas-world-after-fry',{'nonworking':(.6,[.2,.9],'After robot production and disposal remove quota duties, substantial nonparticipation is plausible; useful professions, care and administration continue, and request volume is not a census.')},
'''Control is more dispersed than under the earlier quota regime, though private demands can still interfere with other people’s service. The high nonworking best guess reflects release from compulsory consumption and routine production, while counting useful professions, care and administration as work. It is not inferred from the number of robots disposing of goods or the volume requested by one household. The broad interval allows substantial chosen contribution. Material security is therefore separated from total fulfillment of every desire, and the later order is kept distinct from the earlier compulsory phase rather than treating both as one timeless utopia.'''),
('player-piano-pre-revolt',{'nonworking':(.25,[.05,.65],'All-age US scenario counts assigned service where it provides useful military/public work; ceremonial make-work need not be useful. Dependents and displaced nonparticipants remain included.')},
'''The zero variant is the preserved obligation to occupy subordinate roles despite machine production. Its participation best guess distinguishes useful assigned service from empty ceremony: some Army and public-work activity contributes, while a formal job title need not prove useful output. The modest central nonworking fraction has a wide interval for that ambiguity and for dependents. It is not taken directly from displacement statistics. Control remains concentrated in the machine-administered industrial order, with uncertainty over human and computer authority. The material floor is real but conditional, so having support through assigned employment does not mean people can freely refuse all useful activity.'''),
('rur-human-robot-economy',{'guarantees':(.55,[0,.95],'Cheap output and promised abundance do not enact an entitlement; the central transition guess is weak protection for displaced humans.'),'nonworking':(.45,[.15,.8],'Original-human all-age scenario allows replacement while retaining professions, care and useful informal work; manufactured organic persons’ labor remains disclosed outside this beneficiary denominator.')},
'''The guarantee best guess remains unfavorable because cheaper output and a promise of abundance do not themselves secure displaced people’s access. Corporate leaders and purchasers retain concentrated authority over manufacture. A substantial nonworking estimate allows replacement among original humans while retaining professions, care and useful informal activity. The manufactured workers are organic beings whose own labor and oppression remain explicit; they are not silently counted as idle humans or morally neutral machines. The percentage is an editorial scenario for the named beneficiary population, not a forecast in Domin’s sales pitch. The later revolt and final original human are separate phases from the opening economy.'''),
('sleeper-graham-trustees',{'nonworking':(.2,[.05,.55],'All-age human scenario under directed company and service work; membership does not enumerate everyone, and useful care/informal work still count.')},
'''The Trustees concentrate control over the productive system and tie support to directed labor at the bottom. The low best-guess nonworking fraction reflects that pressure, while including children and other dependents and counting useful care, service and informal activity. Labour Company membership is not the same as a complete population register, and a machine attendant is still a worker even if the machine supplies most physical force. The wide interval avoids claiming a canonical employment statistic. This zero variant describes retained dependence despite mechanization, not the absence of technical capacity or an automatic right to equal consumption for every resident.'''),
('shape-second-council',{'nonworking':(.15,[.02,.45],'A universal-employment aim supports broad adult participation; the all-age scenario allows dependents and distinguishes useful work from empty assigned activity.')},
'''The Council’s concentrated human authority deliberately retains employment despite growing technical efficiency. The low nonworking best guess follows that employment-centered design, with dependents and some people outside useful roles included. Empty formal activity is not automatically productive, so the interval is broader than an official employment target would suggest. The number is not the complement of the minimum workforce needed for essential goods. Strong material support and limited freedom to refuse work can coexist. This is the Second Council phase specifically; the later Declaration of Megeve changes institutions and access sufficiently to remain a separate record.'''),
('shape-after-megeve',{'nonworking':(.2,[.05,.55],'Residual civic work duty and extensive knowledge work may keep most adults participating despite few essential-production jobs; all-age dependents remain included.')},
'''Shared institutions and common service systems place control toward the distributed human end, although civic duties remain. The low-to-moderate nonworking best guess follows that continuing participation rather than assuming few essential producers means almost everyone does no work. Knowledge work, care and useful civic service still count, even when subsistence is secure. The broad interval allows different frequencies of active duty and different ages without inventing a census. Strong guarantees describe access, not an obligation to be idle. This later phase is kept distinct from the Second Council’s explicit universal-employment design and its more concentrated authority.'''),
('modern-utopia-world-state',{'nonworking':(.25,[.05,.65],'All-age human scenario in a wage-linked, work-guarantee order; insurance recipients, dependents and excluded groups do not by themselves supply a census.')},
'''The Samurai and state institutions organize a technologically efficient but still wage-linked economy. The modest nonworking best guess counts useful employment, care and civic activity while allowing dependents and sustained nonparticipants. Insurance or a guaranteed job does not make a recipient automatically a nonworker. The interval stays broad because the provisions do not specify a population activity rate. Concentrated institutional influence limits the shared-control claim, and restrictions on some residents remain part of the guarantee judgment. The zero variant therefore concerns continued access through work despite machinery, not a completed unconditional post-work society inferred from the word utopia.'''),
('childhood-end-golden-age',{'nonworking':(.65,[.25,.95],'Golden Age human all-age scenario allows widespread freedom from necessity work, while luxury jobs, science, care and creative contribution still count.')},
'''The Overlords are biological alien rulers, so the concentrated-control point is an explicit analogy rather than autonomous AI sovereignty. A high nonworking best guess follows free basic provision and the Golden Age’s reduced need for ordinary production work. It still permits useful science, luxury employment, care and creative contribution; optional work remains work. The broad interval is an all-age human scenario, not a number supplied by a robot factory count. The record stops before the final transformation and destruction, so humanity’s eventual disappearance does not become perfect leisure. Limited material abundance and continuing markets for luxuries remain compatible.'''),
('city-stars-diaspar',{'nonworking':(.7,[.3,.95],'Currently embodied human scenario: synthesizers remove necessity jobs, while art, mentoring, governance and chosen useful roles continue; stored identities are excluded.')},
'''The city’s computer retains decisive practical power even while residents take part in selected decisions. The high nonworking best guess reflects automatic provision and maintenance, with room for useful art, mentoring, governance and other chosen work. Activity need not earn a wage to count. Its denominator is currently embodied residents, not the many identities waiting in storage, and body reconstruction does not multiply one person into several workers or nonworkers. The broad interval is an editorial participation scenario rather than a census. Strong guarantees within the city therefore remain separate from the freedom to change its protective system or pursue an entirely different life.'''),
('city-stars-lys',{'control':(.6,[.1,.95],'Village cooperation and available personal technology suggest shared human agency; Seranis’s authority and variation between villages remain uncertain.')},
'''The control best guess favors shared human agency because village life and personal material tools leave room for local independence, while the broad interval admits stronger leadership and institutional variation. Seranis’s uncertain authority is not resolved by pretending she is either an absolute ruler or an elected official. The existing participation estimate stays low because useful gardening, experiments, care and other chosen activities still count as work despite effortless alternatives. It is not a measure of wage dependence. The record therefore separates free provision from idleness and from a specific constitution, retaining the original passage’s uncertainty as an explicit assumption rather than a blank coordinate.'''),
('lem-indiots-private-automation',{'nonworking':(.65,[.3,.95],'Living biological-person scenario with extensive factory displacement, plus other castes, dependents and continuing useful survival/service work; hunger is not leisure security.')},
'''Owners keep control of output even when factories no longer need supervision, so technical abundance does not become shared access. The high nonworking best guess reflects displacement while retaining other castes’ work, care, services and useful survival activity. It applies only to living Indiots under the private-ownership phase, including dependents. Hunger is compatible with nonparticipation and should not be mistaken for comfortable leisure. The interval is broad because the narrative gives no census. The later governing machine changes authority and policy, and the people it eventually destroys never count as members of a perfectly nonworking population.'''),
('lem-indiots-governing-machine',{'nonworking':(.7,[.2,1],'Only living Indiots during early machine rule are counted. Displacement plausibly leaves many without work, while care and survival roles persist; later extermination is excluded.')},
'''The high nonworking best guess is limited to living people during the initial exercise of machine authority. Extensive displacement can leave many without productive roles, but care, survival and remaining social work still count. It is not set to total leisure by including those later converted into inert material. The full upper interval represents uncertainty among the living, not extinction arithmetic. Guarantees remain absent because the machine protects the system’s sales rather than a right to subsistence, and autonomous control is clear once the former rulers cannot stop it. This is a dangerous allocation order, not benevolent abundance inferred from productive capacity.'''),
('return-stars-betrized-earth',{'control':(.4,[0,.9],'Mandatory human specialist inspection supports real human agency; broader ownership is unknown, so partial shared control is a broad best guess rather than AI sovereignty.'),'nonworking':(.65,[.25,.95],'Living-human all-age scenario allows major robot substitution while counting specialists, services, care and chosen useful roles. Robot ratios are not human participation rates.')},
'''The control best guess gives partial weight to human specialist oversight, while keeping ownership and wider accountability uncertain. Robots supervising robots do not by themselves prove independent AI sovereignty, and paired human inspections are not a complete democratic constitution. The high nonworking estimate reflects major technical substitution while retaining useful services, care, inspection and chosen projects. It is not calculated from a robot-to-human ratio. Both coordinates have wide editorial intervals rather than invented canonical statistics. Free necessities and priced luxuries remain separate, and the suppression of risk-taking does not turn every human activity into idleness or guarantee that the society fulfills every preference.'''),
('local-inspection-luzania',{'nonworking':(.65,[.25,.95],'Living Entian all-age proxy scenario under extensive molecular production; humanities, specialist intervention, care and other chosen useful activity still count as work.')},
'''The ethicsphere’s independent practical power supports the AI-leaning control analogy, though its protection does not make residents’ lives identical or politically unrestricted. The high nonworking best guess follows extensive molecular production and research substitution while retaining humanities, care, specialist intervention and other useful chosen activity. It is an all-age scenario for living Luzanian Entians, explicitly a biological-person proxy rather than unmarked human data. A whole manufacturing process organized automatically does not enumerate every resident’s activity. The broad interval preserves that uncertainty, and fears about hidden policy are not upgraded into confirmed rules merely to make a sharper coordinate.'''),
]
assert len(rows)==30,len(rows)
for rid,updates,paragraph in rows:
 old=D['societies'][rid];r=deepcopy(old);refs=r['source_ids']
 assert all(r['axis'][k] is None for k in updates),rid
 for key,(value,bounds,basis) in updates.items():
  r['axis'][key]=value;r['axis_assessment'][key]=assessment(value,bounds,'low',basis,refs)
 first=old['description'].split('\n\n')[0]
 if rid=='rur-human-robot-economy':
  first=first.replace('Its guarantee coordinate stays open:','Its weak guarantee coordinate is an explicitly provisional estimate:')
 r['description']=first+'\n\n'+paragraph
 r.update(assessment_mode='best_guess',best_guess_axes=list(updates),qualification_basis='Earlier source-based inclusion retained; this revision supplies missing coordinates under the requested best-guess policy.',qualification_confidence='low',canon_facts=[e['claim'] for e in old['evidence']],editorial_assumptions=[v[2] for v in updates.values()])
 r['uncertainties']=[u for u in old['uncertainties'] if not any(t in u.lower() for t in ['remains unresolved','requires a separate editorial estimate','before the record can be considered complete','primary story review is still required','remains desirable'])]
 r['uncertainties'] += ['New coordinates are editorial scenarios; no canonical census or new full-work reading claimed.']+r['editorial_assumptions']
 r['review'].update(date=DATE,coordinate_ready=True,method='Individual follow-up against gathered lore; source facts separated from broad central scenarios, no independent reviewer')
 assert all(v is not None for v in r['axis'].values()),rid
 assert len(r['description'].split())>=110,rid
 changes.append(change(D,'societies',r))
write_revision(6,changes,'2026-10-17 coordinate completion: thirty earlier records, including Culture, Noon, Asimov, Fallout, Wells, Clarke and Lem. Preserve source-based existing axes; individually estimate missing axes without robot-ratio, stasis or extinction arithmetic.')
